Standard word-count exercise. Implementation: split the input into words, treating characters other than alphanumeric and apostrophe as separators. Trim leading/trailing apostrophes from each token, lowercase it, and count.

Note: Some tests have `#[ignore]` attached — but the task says to make the tests pass. The tests use `output.remove(word).unwrap_or(0)`, so they only check the expected keys and the emptiness of the remainder. Actually, the tests check that the output after removing the expected keys is empty, so extra keys will fail. But the ignored tests won't run. Should I remove the `#[ignore]`? No — "do not modify the tests." So I just need to implement it correctly. `cargo test` runs the non-ignored tests, but I should make sure all tests pass including the ignored ones (run with `--ignored` to verify).

